  "title": "Slashing Amount Not Accounted for in Net Staking Limit Check",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nIn the `StakingManager::stake` function the protocol enforces a staking limit by calculating the `netStaked` amount as:\n\n```solidity\n\ncontract StakingManager {\n    // [...]\n\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Stakes HYPE tokens and mints kHYPE tokens\n     * @dev Can be called directly or via the receive function\n     */\n    function stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n        // [...]\n        if (stakingLimit > 0) {\n            // Get rewards from ValidatorManager to account for earned rewards\n            // This approach uses global rewards but provides a reasonable approximation\n            // for this StakingManager's available capacity\n            uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n@>          uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed;\n            require(netStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit, \"Staking limit reached\");\n        }\n\n        // [...]\n    }\n\n   \n}\n\n\n```\n\nHowever, it does not subtract the `slashingAmount` of a validator, which leads to an overestimated `netStaked` value. This, in turn, underestimates the remaining staking capacity of a validator. As a result, **new stake attempts may be incorrectly rejected despite the validator having sufficient actual capacity**.\n\nSo let's say a validator has a staking limit of `100 HYPE`.\n- A: stakes `50 HYPE`\n- B: stakes `20 HYPE`\n- totalStaked = `70 HYPE`\n\nIf the validator is slashed `20 HYPE`, the effective stake is now only `50 HYPE`. However, since slashing isn’t deducted in `netStaked`, the protocol still considers it as `70 HYPE`, leaving only `30 HYPE` of capacity, when it should be `50 HYPE`.\n\nThis miscalculation can lead to denial of service for users trying to stake and results in inefficient utilization of the protocol’s staking limits.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nMake sure to add the `slashingAmount` in the `netStake` calculation\n\n```diff\n function stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n        // [...]\n        if (stakingLimit > 0) {\n            // Get rewards from ValidatorManager to account for earned rewards\n            // This approach uses global rewards but provides a reasonable approximation\n            // for this StakingManager's available capacity\n            uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n+           uint256 slashingAmount = validatorManager.totalSlashing();\n+           uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed - slashingAmount;\n-           uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed;\n            require(netStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit, \"Staking limit reached\");\n        }\n\n        // [...]\n    }\n```",
